{# =============================================================================
   tmsm.ui v1 â€” widget macros
   Import in a TemplateView template (the `with context` is REQUIRED â€” without
   it Jinja isolates macro scope and `{{ id }}` renders empty, which silently
   breaks every click handler):
       {% import 'tmsm_ui/widgets.xml' as ui with context %}
   Conventions:
     * Every macro reads `id` from the surrounding context (provided by BaseView).
     * Every action fires the signal named in `name` -> handler connected via
       `self.connect("name", handler)` on the Python side.
     * Labels never carry `action`/`scriptevents`; the underlying quad does.
       This lets the hover script see MouseOver events on the quad and look
       it up by `id` (TM2020 ManiaScript has no working `HasClass`).
     * Button names within a single view MUST be unique â€” the macro emits an
       `id` derived from the name and `Page.GetFirstChild` returns only the
       first match.
   ============================================================================ #}

